\vspace{0.22cm}
{\Large\bfseries\color{ChapterCrimson} 全書一句話 \textperiodcentered\ The Whole Book in One Verse}

\vspace{0.30cm}
\fcolorbox{ScriptureGold}{ScriptureBg}{%
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\centering\vspace{0.2cm}
\normalsize\color{CommentaryBrown}
當時，雲彩遮蓋會幕，耶和華的\textbf{\color{GloryGold!80!black}榮光}就\textbf{\color{GloryGold!80!black}充滿}了帳幕。\\
摩西不能進會幕；因為雲彩停在其上，並且耶和華的榮光充滿了帳幕。\\[0.5em]
\footnotesize\itshape
Then the cloud covered the tent of meeting, and the \textbf{glory} of the LORD
\textbf{filled} the tabernacle.\\
Moses was not able to enter the tent of meeting because the cloud had settled
on it, and the glory of the LORD filled the tabernacle.\\[0.4em]
\small\color{ChapterCrimson} 出埃及記 40:34-35 \textperiodcentered\ Exodus 40:34-35
\vspace{0.2cm}
\end{minipage}}

\vspace{0.35cm}
{\small\color{TextGray} 四十章 \textperiodcentered\ 七卷 \textperiodcentered\ 一句從奴役到同住的宣告\\
\textit{Forty chapters \textperiodcentered\ seven volumes \textperiodcentered\ one declaration from bondage to dwelling}}

\vspace{0.30cm}
{\small
\renewcommand{\arraystretch}{1.3}
\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.8cm}p{2.4cm}p{6.9cm}@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{段落} & \textbf{章節} & \textbf{在全書的展開} \\
\midrule
為奴之地與蒙召的僕人 & 1-6章 & 以色列在埃及為奴受苦，神紀念祂的約，呼召摩西作拯救者 \\
十災與逾越的羔羊 & 7-13章 & 耶和華審判埃及的假神，以羔羊的血分別祂的百姓，設立逾越節 \\
過紅海與曠野路 & 14-18章 & 神在海中開路、在曠野降糧供水，帶百姓走向西奈山 \\
西奈之約與律法 & 19-24章 & 神在西奈顯現，賜下十誡與律例，百姓立約甘心順從 \\
會幕的藍圖 & 25-31章 & 神吩咐建造會幕，為要在百姓中間有一個可安居之處 \\
金牛犢與立約的更新 & 32-34章 & 百姓背約拜金牛犢，摩西代求，神更新祂的約 \\
建造與榮耀充滿 & 35-40章 & 百姓甘心奉獻，會幕照著吩咐建成，耶和華的榮光親自入住 \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
}

\vspace{0.4cm}
\textcolor{ScriptureGold}{\rule{2.5in}{0.7pt}}
\vspace{0.3cm}

{\bfseries\color{ChapterCrimson} 讀經之鑰 \textperiodcentered\ How to Read This Book}

\vspace{0.18cm}
\begin{minipage}{4.6in}
\small\color{TextGray}
不是來讀一部逃出埃及的歷史，是來看神如何救贖一群奴僕，使他們成為可以與祂同住的百姓。\\
若你讀完四十章卻只記得「十災」與「十誡」——請從頭再讀，\\
這次留意：全書的終點不是紅海的勝利，也不是西奈山的律法，而是40:34那朵雲彩——神甘願住在祂所救贖之人的中間。\\[0.5em]
\textit{\footnotesize
You are not reading a history of an escape from Egypt — you are watching how
God redeems a nation of slaves so that He may dwell among them.\\
If after forty chapters you remember only "the ten plagues" and "the ten
commandments," read it again.\\
This time notice: the book's destination is not the victory at the sea, nor
the law given at Sinai, but the cloud of 40:34 — God willing to dwell in the
midst of the people He has redeemed.}
\end{minipage}

\vfill
{\scriptsize\color{LightGray} PubHub 三書精讀系統 \textperiodcentered\ Soli Deo Gloria}

